	"id": "ombuwomo",
	"name": "Ombuwomo",
	"codex": {
		"entry": "A round bud of the Ombulumo, its spotted leaves folded shut around a soft body that peeks out between the front two. It has no legs: it hops and rocks its way over the wet ground of the shallows, and sits as still as a stone when it rests. In time it ascends into an Ombulumo. Its name is a beast-call, the sound of it: the Ombulumo's round start, with a soft w in the middle, the leaves wrapped round.",
		"gloss": "the folded boom"
	},
